01:13:07,234 --> 01:13:08,234
Where are you?

1034
01:13:08,683 --> 01:13:11,624
You never would've gotten
on that plane if I told you.

1035
01:13:14,731 --> 01:13:17,734
But you said that you'd be
here Darling, listen to me.

1036
01:13:18,307 --> 01:13:20,497
Do you understand how
much strength it gives me

1037
01:13:21,112 --> 01:13:22,843
knowing that you will survive?

1038
01:13:24,626 --> 01:13:30,351
The only thing left to do
now, is tell the truth to people.

1039
01:13:31,466 --> 01:13:39,047
At least if they know, families
can say goodbye to each other.

1040
01:13:40,225 --> 01:13:42,936
A mother can comfort her children.

1041
01:13:45,522 --> 01:13:46,638
And a father.

1042
01:13:49,547 --> 01:13:51,883
Can ask his daughter for forgiveness.

1043
01:14:01,653 --> 01:14:03,352
Whenever you're ready, Mr President.

1044
01:14:12,361 --> 01:14:17,961
My fellow Americans this will
be the last time I address you.

1045
01:14:19,369 --> 01:14:23,988
As you know, catastrophe
has struck our nation.

1046
01:14:25,781 --> 01:14:27,439
Has struck the world.

1047
01:14:28,273 --> 01:14:32,819
I wish I could tell you we could
prevent the coming destruction.

1048
01:14:34,102 --> 01:14:35,291
We cannot.

1049
01:14:36,490 --> 01:14:38,971
Today, none of us are strangers.

1050
01:14:40,264 --> 01:14:46,406
Today, we are one family,
stepping into the darkness together.

1051
01:14:47,198 --> 01:14:49,826
We are a nation of many religions,

1052
01:14:50,358 --> 01:14:56,260
But I believe these
words reflect the spirit.

1053
01:14:57,104 --> 01:14:59,082
"The Lord is my shepard."

1054
01:14:59,106 --> 01:15:00,138
I shall.

1055
01:15:02,005 --> 01:15:04,706
People! Get away from
the doors and windows.

1056
01:15:05,581 --> 01:15:07,531
What are we gonna do? You tell me.

1057
01:15:07,886 --> 01:15:10,753
Dr Silberman? Tamara!

1058
01:15:10,930 --> 01:15:12,463
What are you doing here?

1059
01:15:13,360 --> 01:15:14,643
She's a patient, honey.

1060
01:15:14,799 --> 01:15:18,059
Excuse me, I have a
private plane out there.

1061
01:15:18,083 --> 01:15:20,148
Karpov! Yuri!

1062
01:15:20,732 --> 01:15:23,599
You knew. This whole time you knew.

1063
01:15:23,777 --> 01:15:26,237
You've got a way out of
here, right? You got a plane?

1064
01:15:26,477 --> 01:15:28,813
My family, take us with you. Please!

1065
01:15:29,157 --> 01:15:30,805
Boss, Boss.

1066
01:15:31,305 --> 01:15:33,359
I found us a plane. An Antonov.

1067
01:15:33,422 --> 01:15:35,786
They were just about to take
off, but the tower didn't let them.

1068
01:15:35,810 --> 01:15:38,197
Can you still fly that thing?

1069
01:15:38,541 --> 01:15:41,638
Sure, Boss, but I need co-pilot.

1070
01:15:42,660 --> 01:15:43,765
Gordon's a pilot.

1071
01:15:45,423 --> 01:15:47,425
No, I'm not.

1072
01:15:47,530 --> 01:15:49,730
Yes he is. Great pilot. Let's go.

1073
01:15:50,261 --> 01:15:52,076
Good. Let's go!

1074
01:15:52,399 --> 01:15:55,287
Jackson, stop saying I'm a pilot.

1075
01:15:57,467 --> 01:15:59,125
You can't go out there. Come back!

1076
01:16:05,162 --> 01:16:06,601
Move back, People!

1077
01:16:13,326 --> 01:16:15,193
Wow, that's a big plane.

1078
01:16:16,183 --> 01:16:17,518
It's Russian.

1079
01:16:18,967 --> 01:16:20,594
Let's move everybody. Come on!

1080
01:16:26,193 --> 01:16:28,508
Gordon, where are you? Let's go!

1081
01:16:28,696 --> 01:16:30,604
Up here, Gordon. Hurry up!

1082
01:16:32,189 --> 01:16:34,524
Oh my God.***

1083
01:16:42,147 --> 01:16:45,543
Woah, Look at these. Las Vegas auto show.

1084
01:16:45,567 --> 01:16:48,851
We had VIP tickets for this.

1085
01:16:49,060 --> 01:16:50,520
That's fantastic, Let's go.

1086
01:16:50,551 --> 01:16:53,252
Check the main bus for
hydraulics, I'll balance the tanks.

1087
01:16:53,345 --> 01:16:54,345
What?

1088
01:16:56,359 --> 01:16:58,340
Okay, okay. I'm trying.

1089
01:17:00,832 --> 01:17:02,518
Tower to Antonov, what
the hell are you doing?

1090
01:17:02,542 --> 01:17:04,304
Shut down immediately.

1091
01:17:11,895 --> 01:17:12,893
Caesar, shh.

1092
01:17:12,917 --> 01:17:14,419
When I say "go".

1093
01:17:14,481 --> 01:17:16,671
We push all this down at once, okay?

1094
01:17:16,723 --> 01:17:18,016
Okay. Go!

1095
01:17:18,256 --> 01:17:22,260
Antonov, abort take-off.
You do not have clearance.

1096
01:17:22,385 --> 01:17:24,189
I repeat, you must abort.

1097
01:17:31,164 --> 01:17:32,164
What the hell was that?

1098
01:17:32,332 --> 01:17:34,261
I don't know, but it's not good.

1099
01:17:37,316 --> 01:17:39,590
Push! Pushing! Come on!

1100
01:17:43,875 --> 01:17:45,345
We're going down!

1101
01:17:54,959 --> 01:17:57,000
It must be thetake over.

1102
01:17:57,024 --> 01:17:58,984
Take over, What do you mean, take over?

1103
01:18:02,039 --> 01:18:03,791
Sasha! Relax.

1104
01:18:04,041 --> 01:18:05,041
Now!

1105
01:18:08,754 --> 01:18:10,850
God, God, Jesus.

1106
01:18:14,228 --> 01:18:16,040
Oh, God

1107
01:18:16,064 --> 01:18:18,775
Sasha, now! Take a deep breath.

1108
01:18:19,098 --> 01:18:20,412
Pull!

1109
01:18:22,862 --> 01:18:26,230
Come up, baby.

1110
01:18:47,772 --> 01:18:49,065
Was that the Eiffel Tower?

1111
01:18:50,358 --> 01:18:51,537
I think so.

1112
01:18:59,701 --> 01:19:03,413
Ladies and gentlemen.
We're on our way to China.

1113
01:19:06,103 --> 01:19:08,439
Good. Very good.

1114
01:19:18,991 --> 01:19:22,901
Do not believe in something simply
because you have heard it, Nima.

1115
01:19:24,215 --> 01:19:27,187
But Great Lama. Tenzin is my brother.

1116
01:19:28,125 --> 01:19:30,899
He works inside the big
tunnel, where the ships are built.

1117
01:19:34,110 --> 01:19:38,761
But what is there in your wisdom,
Great Lama, if Tenzin is right?

1118
01:19:39,376 --> 01:19:41,701
What if our world is
indeed coming to and end?

1119
01:19:51,847 --> 01:19:57,154
It is full, Great Rinpoche.

1120
01:20:01,075 --> 01:20:08,207
Like this cup, you are full
of opinions and speculations.

1121
01:20:08,739 --> 01:20:13,431
To see the light of wisdom,
you first must empty your cup.

1122
01:20:31,365 --> 01:20:32,700
Be careful with the clutch.

1123
01:20:33,618 --> 01:20:35,766
It tends to slip.

1124
01:20:53,805 --> 01:20:57,350
Grandma Grandpa, Nima is here!

1125
01:20:57,527 --> 01:20:59,258
Grandma, I got a message from Tenzin.

1126
01:20:59,592 --> 01:21:02,636
He want us to meet him in
Cho Ming at the work camp.

1127
01:21:03,189 --> 01:21:06,231
He says he can get us onto
the ships he's working on.

1128
01:21:06,255 --> 01:21:08,285
What are you talking about?

1129
01:21:08,309 --> 01:21:10,509
Tenzin works on the dam.

1130
01:21:13,887 --> 01:21:14,887
Grandma

1131
01:21:15,472 --> 01:21:19,059
the dam is a ship. The
government lied to us.

1132
01:21:19,455 --> 01:21:21,259
There will be a big flood!

1133
01:21:22,031 --> 01:21:23,884
We must pack up right away.

1134
01:21:23,908 --> 01:21:27,533
Nima? Who gave you a truck? Grandpa.

1135
01:21:27,557 --> 01:21:34,105
We took a trip on the liam song ferry
once grandpa threw up the whole way.

1136
01:21:34,981 --> 01:21:36,462
Let's eat first.

1137
01:21:42,885 --> 01:21:46,336
Hey, Look, the new Bentley!
Our father had one on order.

1138
01:21:46,576 --> 01:21:48,557
He was supposed to get it next year.

1139
01:21:48,964 --> 01:21:51,571
But then he canceled
it. Because of the ships.

1140
01:21:52,509 --> 01:21:54,417
How many cars does your family have?

1141
01:21:55,731 --> 01:21:57,837
My Mom's boyfriend has a Porsche.

1142
01:21:58,859 --> 01:22:00,632
Our parents are divorced too.

1143
01:22:00,663 --> 01:22:03,416
Yeah, but there is nothing
that we can do about that.

1144
01:22:03,447 --> 01:22:04,447
Found a hat.

1145
01:22:05,418 --> 01:22:06,648
She has a thing for hats.

1146
01:22:07,462 --> 01:22:09,370
I was just like that at her age.

1147
01:22:09,975 --> 01:22:11,403
They made me feel safe.

1148
01:22:12,811 --> 01:22:15,918
So, how did you meet Dr Silberman?

1149
01:22:17,138 --> 01:22:19,119
As you can see not the same way you did.

1150
01:22:21,257 --> 01:22:26,481
My boyfriend asked me to get them
done. But he's not your husband?

1151
01:22:26,793 --> 01:22:29,077
Oh, no, We are not married.

1152
01:22:29,192 --> 01:22:30,860
And probably never will be.

1153
01:22:39,056 --> 01:22:40,056
For the boys.

1154
01:22:45,385 --> 01:22:47,283
They seem to like each other.

1155
01:22:49,556 --> 01:22:50,849
Yeah, I guess.

1156
01:22:53,059 --> 01:22:55,291
Tell me, Mr Karpov, how much did you pay?

1157
01:22:56,698 --> 01:23:00,118
One billion Euro. Per seat.

1158
01:23:02,141 --> 01:23:04,435
That's disgusting Oh yeah?

1159
01:23:05,791 --> 01:23:09,315
You know, Curtis, I wasn't
always a businessman.

1160
01:23:09,816 --> 01:23:11,620
I am a boxer.

1161
01:23:12,193 --> 01:23:15,863
Was my only playing when I
was boy back in Murmansk.

1162
01:23:15,968 --> 01:23:20,065
And my coach, his name was also Yuri.

1163
01:23:20,389 --> 01:23:25,905
He always say "If
someone wants to beat you"

1164
01:23:26,051 --> 01:23:28,115
"he has to kill you first."

1165
01:23:32,046 --> 01:23:33,068
That's very nice.

1166
01:23:33,756 --> 01:23:40,586
Yeah. But tell me, what would you
have done if you were rich like me?

1167
01:23:41,128 --> 01:23:44,048
Look, they are wonderful children.

1168
01:23:46,342 --> 01:23:51,149
Ok guys. The plan is to refill in
Hawaii, so sit down and buckle up.

1169
01:23:51,576 --> 01:23:52,827
Gordon and I will do the rest.

1170
01:23:56,352 --> 01:23:57,352
Oh God.

1171
01:23:59,542 --> 01:24:00,669
Go get the guys.

1172
01:24:04,454 --> 01:24:07,279
Guys, there's ayou might wanna.

1173
01:24:26,038 --> 01:24:30,261
What is that? The state of Hawaii.

1174
01:24:30,688 --> 01:24:34,536
Not good. That is not good.

1175
01:24:39,708 --> 01:24:41,094
How much fuel do we have left?

1176
01:24:41,637 --> 01:24:42,637
Not enough.

1177
01:24:43,086 --> 01:24:46,881
We have to make a water landing
somewhere in south China sea.

1178
01:24:47,267 --> 01:24:49,843
Great, at least we won't
need a landing gear.

1179
01:24:49,989 --> 01:24:52,835
What about it? We lost it all, in Vegas.

1180
01:25:04,472 --> 01:25:05,838
Dr Wilson, may I come in?

1181
01:25:06,693 --> 01:25:08,799
I'm not very good company, I'm afraid.

1182
01:25:10,144 --> 01:25:12,949
Doctor Please, call me Adrian.

1183
01:25:18,882 --> 01:25:20,624
All those people we left behind.

1184
01:25:21,927 --> 01:25:23,647
They don't stand a chance, do they?

1185
01:25:25,910 --> 01:25:29,716
I believe that nature will
choose for itself, from itself,

1186
01:25:29,987 --> 01:25:31,176
What will survive.

1187
01:25:33,053 --> 01:25:35,857
Just like you, preserving
those great artworks.

1188
01:25:37,067 --> 01:25:40,737
Our culture is our soul,
and that's not dying tonight.

1189
01:25:40,852 --> 01:25:44,429
Come on, I contributed to this cover up.

1190
01:25:45,231 --> 01:25:48,307
The Da Vinci, Picasso, they're in.

1191
01:25:48,683 --> 01:25:50,431
But if you're some nobody
you don't stand a chance.

1192
01:25:50,455 --> 01:25:54,272
It's not necessarily true.

1193
01:25:55,878 --> 01:25:59,725
Did you ever hear of a
writer called Jackson Curtis?

1194
01:26:00,121 --> 01:26:01,998
Wrote a book, "Farewell Atlantis".

1195
01:26:03,103 --> 01:26:05,738
What do you think the chances
are of an unknown writer.

1196
01:26:05,762 --> 01:26:09,026
Who barely sold 500 copies
making it aboard this plane?

1197
01:26:11,111 --> 01:26:15,112
I don't understand I mean
call it chance or faith or nature,

1198
01:26:15,136 --> 01:26:19,005
Doesn't matter this book is
part of our legacy now. Why?

1199
01:26:20,152 --> 01:26:21,424
Because I'm reading it.

1200
01:26:25,835 --> 01:26:29,192
Dr Helmsley, please
report to the situation room.

1201
01:26:42,038 --> 01:26:42,994
Who is it?

1202
01:26:43,018 --> 01:26:46,543
Hello, I'm sorry. Who is this?

1203
01:26:46,616 --> 01:26:48,211
This is Yoko Delgado.

1204
01:26:48,639 --> 01:26:50,526
Do you want to speak to my Daddy?

1205
01:26:53,852 --> 01:26:54,968
Yes, please.

1206
01:26:55,427 --> 01:26:56,918
Who should I say is calling?

1207
01:27:01,026 --> 01:27:05,854
Tell him, its his father.
You're my grandpa?

1208
01:27:06,980 --> 01:27:08,388
Yes, sweetheart, I am.

1209
01:27:11,192 --> 01:27:13,288
Daddy, grandpa is on the phone.

1210
01:28:17,446 --> 01:28:18,718
Mr President, Sir.

1211
01:28:26,466 --> 01:28:29,104
What's the matter, sweety?
She can't find her Daddy.

1212
01:28:31,877 --> 01:28:34,547
Why don't you two get comfy on that couch?

1213
01:28:34,839 --> 01:28:36,267
Sally, come here

1214
01:28:38,040 --> 01:28:39,468
I'll find your Daddy.

1215
01:28:47,914 --> 01:28:49,267
Who can help me with missing persons?

1216
01:28:49,291 --> 01:28:51,053
Sorry, man, I'm really busy right now.

1217
01:28:52,846 --> 01:28:56,534
I mean of course, sir. Sorry, Mr President.

1218
01:28:56,558 --> 01:28:58,769
Don't worry about it,
you're doing a great job, son.

1219
01:29:25,712 --> 01:29:27,961
What's happening? The
capital has been hit by a 9.4.

1220
01:29:27,985 --> 01:29:29,557
Lost communication
with the White House, sir.

1221
01:29:29,581 --> 01:29:31,791
Where is it centered? North Chesapeake bay.

1222
01:29:36,421 --> 01:29:39,653
Mr Anheuser, Russian
president on the line, sir.

1223
01:29:40,269 --> 01:29:41,269
Excuse me.

1224
01:29:42,083 --> 01:29:43,730
We just entered Chinese air space.

1225
01:29:45,920 --> 01:29:47,307
That's affirmative, Mr President.

1226
01:29:47,849 --> 01:29:52,812
Until communication is restored,
I suppose I am in command.

1227
01:29:53,720 --> 01:29:56,052
It appears that all other
heads of state are en route,

1228
01:29:56,076 --> 01:29:58,547
With the exception of
the Italian Prime Minister,

1229
01:29:59,454 --> 01:30:04,094
Who has also decided to
stay behind and trust in prayer.

1230
01:31:11,412 --> 01:31:13,650
Earths crust has begun
to shift, Dr Helmsley!

1231
01:31:13,674 --> 01:31:16,612
By what degree? 1.2 degree. Still moving.

1232
01:31:16,636 --> 01:31:17,991
So, what happens next?

1233
01:31:18,137 --> 01:31:20,734
The movement of our land
masses comes to a halt.

1234
01:31:20,848 --> 01:31:22,183
Let's see a simulation.

1235
01:31:23,393 --> 01:31:25,697
Expect the formation of gigantic tsunamis.

1236
01:31:25,853 --> 01:31:28,314
Proportional to the magnitude
of corresponding quakes.

1237
01:31:34,195 --> 01:31:35,968
Pull up the Japanese sea border.

1238
01:31:36,145 --> 01:31:37,145
Yes, sir.

1239
01:31:38,324 --> 01:31:40,295
My Dad's on a cruise ship out there.

1240
01:31:41,963 --> 01:31:43,798
But I guess you already knew that.

1241
01:31:45,498 --> 01:31:47,622
Sir, we've recorded two underwater quakes.

1242
01:31:47,646 --> 01:31:49,439
At 7.9 and 8.2.

1243
01:32:06,936 --> 01:32:08,268
From what we have just learned,

1244
01:32:08,292 --> 01:32:11,753
Tokyo seems to have taken
the full force of the earthquake.

1245
01:32:11,910 --> 01:32:14,044
At this point unconfirmed
reports Indicate that.

1246
01:32:14,068 --> 01:32:16,811
Large areas of land are under water.

1247
01:32:17,123 --> 01:32:18,719
Please stay tuned for further.

1248
01:32:29,021 --> 01:32:32,316
Tony I called.

1249
01:32:36,486 --> 01:32:37,717
I was too late.

1250
01:32:42,586 --> 01:32:45,037
Maybe they got out of town.

1251
01:32:46,027 --> 01:32:47,445
You never know.

1252
01:34:15,523 --> 01:34:17,473
I'm coming home, Dorothy.

1253
01:34:44,458 --> 01:34:45,458
Anything?

1254
01:34:47,357 --> 01:34:48,483
Nothing but static.

1255
01:34:49,046 --> 01:34:50,621
Not even an emergency signal.

1256
01:35:04,207 --> 01:35:06,272
Can't think about what's
going on down there.

1257
01:35:13,769 --> 01:35:15,750
Remember that old
beetle we used to camp in?

1258
01:35:15,896 --> 01:35:17,176
But you'd never get the roof up.

1259
01:35:19,660 --> 01:35:20,932
We definitely traded up.

1260
01:35:24,634 --> 01:35:26,563
I tried to find our old
spot at Yellowstone.

1261
01:35:27,022 --> 01:35:28,784
When I went camping with the kids, but.

1262
01:35:30,171 --> 01:35:31,245
I couldn't find it.

1263
01:35:40,327 --> 01:35:41,755
Do you think people change?

1264
01:35:43,131 --> 01:35:44,414
By people, do you mean me?

1265
01:35:44,956 --> 01:35:45,956
Yes.

1266
01:35:46,072 --> 01:35:48,053
Do you think you've
changed since we separated?

1267
01:35:50,399 --> 01:35:52,140
I seem to eat a lot more cereal now.

1268
01:35:56,801 --> 01:35:58,334
You always had tunnel vision.

1269
01:35:59,794 --> 01:36:01,900
You could just block
everything out and write.

1270
01:36:06,488 --> 01:36:07,792
You blocked us out.

1271
01:36:17,739 --> 01:36:18,739
Do you love him?

1272
01:36:22,035 --> 01:36:23,088
I love him enough.

1273
01:36:36,372 --> 01:36:38,802
All global ground
communication is ceased, sir.

1274
01:36:43,567 --> 01:36:47,258
The only signals our satellites
are picking up from Cho Ming.

1275
01:36:48,958 --> 01:36:50,376
Well there's a piece of good news.

1276
01:36:51,252 --> 01:36:52,461
Any updates, Doctor?

1277
01:36:52,659 --> 01:36:55,920
We expect the tsunamis to
reach land fall on every continent.

1278
01:36:55,944 --> 01:36:59,531
The Cho Ming area will be
impacted in approximately 6 hours.

1279
01:37:01,043 --> 01:37:02,416
It looks like the crust have shifted.

1280
01:37:02,440 --> 01:37:05,391
By almost 23 degrees to the southwest.

1281
01:37:06,308 --> 01:37:10,688
The data also shows the earth's poles
have reversed their magnetic fields.

1282
01:37:11,459 --> 01:37:14,264
These are their new positions. See here?***

1283
01:37:15,985 --> 01:37:20,729
You're telling me that the north
pole is now somewhere in Wisconsin?

1284
01:37:21,323 --> 01:37:23,763
Actually, that's the south pole now.

1285
01:37:32,387 --> 01:37:34,740
Engine failure. 2 of 6 are down.

1286
01:37:34,764 --> 01:37:36,078
You must get ready.

1287
01:37:37,871 --> 01:37:40,749
How long do we have? 18 minutes. Maybe.

1288
01:37:43,366 --> 01:37:44,555
Better wake up the kids.

1289
01:38:25,794 --> 01:38:27,202
Why do you hate Gordon?

1290
01:38:31,873 --> 01:38:34,782
Hey. Come on.

1291
01:38:36,763 --> 01:38:40,225
What are you talking
about? I don't hate him.

1292
01:38:40,663 --> 01:38:45,543
You don't like him either. That's
because I don't know him well, maybe.

1293
01:38:45,699 --> 01:38:46,982
But I do.

1294
01:38:47,211 --> 01:38:49,610
He's really nice once you get to know him.

1295
01:38:49,651 --> 01:38:51,011
You should talk to him more often.

1296
01:38:51,372 --> 01:38:53,426
You guys would get along really well.

1297
01:38:57,743 --> 01:38:58,848
You like him a lot, huh?

1298
01:39:08,097 --> 01:39:10,870
I'll do my best. I promise. Ok?

1299
01:39:12,768 --> 01:39:16,021
I'm really proud of you.
Really proud of you.

1300
01:39:18,065 --> 01:39:21,954
Is it time? Yeah.

1301
01:39:26,188 --> 01:39:27,188
Dad, what's wrong?

1302
01:39:28,159 --> 01:39:30,658
Sasha's gotta land. It's
gonna be a little bumpy.

1303
01:39:30,682 --> 01:39:31,745
Maybe a little wet.

1304
01:39:33,132 --> 01:39:34,132
Daddy?

1305
01:39:40,546 --> 01:39:41,620
Hold her steady.

1306
01:39:59,607 --> 01:40:01,984
Daddy, I'm not a really good swimmer.

1307
01:40:02,276 --> 01:40:05,967
Hey, that's alright. It's
what you got this for.

1308
01:40:06,572 --> 01:40:08,021
It's like being in a swimming pool.

1309
01:40:08,063 --> 01:40:12,526
Only it's got more cool
stuff. It's got a whistle, a light.

1310
01:40:13,224 --> 01:40:14,705
I thought we were going to China.

1311
01:40:16,196 --> 01:40:17,531
No, we gotta land here.

1312
01:40:21,483 --> 01:40:22,136
So that's what we're gonna do.

1313
01:40:22,160 --> 01:40:23,840
We're just gonna all stay together. Right?

1314
01:40:23,871 --> 01:40:25,087
No we're not, we're gonna die!

1315
01:40:25,111 --> 01:40:27,134
No, we're not.

1316
01:40:27,489 --> 01:40:28,489
Promise?

1317
01:40:28,813 --> 01:40:32,254
I promise you, we'll all stay
together, no matter what happens.

1318
01:40:48,124 --> 01:40:49,124
Jackson,

1319
01:40:50,074 --> 01:40:51,074
Yuri.

1320
01:40:52,545 --> 01:40:53,825
I think you better come up here.

1321
01:40:55,141 --> 01:40:56,702
Hold on, hold on. I'm
gonna go check this out.

1322
01:40:56,726 --> 01:40:58,947
Dad, Dad! I'll be right back.

1323
01:41:00,146 --> 01:41:01,846
We gotta buckle up. Let's go.

1324
01:41:03,785 --> 01:41:06,744
Don't ask me how that
happened. There is no more ocean,

1325
01:41:06,768 --> 01:41:09,155
And we're pretty close
to where we wanted to go.

1326
01:41:09,249 --> 01:41:11,415
It's like the whole world
shifted by 1000 miles.

1327
01:41:11,439 --> 01:41:14,168
1578 to be exact.

1328
01:41:14,192 --> 01:41:16,903
It's called "Earth crust
displacement theory".

1329
01:41:16,986 --> 01:41:18,727
Professor Hapgood 1958.

1330
01:41:20,219 --> 01:41:21,532
Way to go, Charlie.

1331
01:41:25,265 --> 01:41:26,265
What was that?

1332
01:41:27,465 --> 01:41:29,634
We just lost our last two engines.

1333
01:41:48,632 --> 01:41:51,427
I'll shoot for that glacier.
It's going to get rocky.

1334
01:41:51,687 --> 01:41:55,306
Listen, it's gonna sound crazy,
but here's what you have to do.

1335
01:41:59,560 --> 01:42:03,084
Get up! Follow me!

1336
01:42:03,157 --> 01:42:05,368
Yuri, what are you doing?

1337
01:42:05,618 --> 01:42:08,037
We are taking the Bentley!

1338
01:42:09,393 --> 01:42:11,843
Not yet! Not yet.

1339
01:42:12,333 --> 01:42:15,055
Almost there.

1340
01:42:16,452 --> 01:42:17,452
Get in the car.

1341
01:42:28,161 --> 01:42:30,664
Okay, go now! Pull!

1342
01:42:35,408 --> 01:42:37,723
No no no no no.

1343
01:42:41,654 --> 01:42:42,443
Go, Jackson.

1344
01:42:42,467 --> 01:42:44,344
We gotta wait for Sasha and Gordon.

1345
01:42:45,721 --> 01:42:49,412
Go! Make sure everybody gets
off the plane before I touch down.

1346
01:42:49,474 --> 01:42:50,474
What about you?

1347
01:42:50,934 --> 01:42:54,302
I'll be fine. I have to
touch this plane down.

1348
01:42:55,825 --> 01:43:00,048
What are you waiting for? Go!

1349
01:43:14,875 --> 01:43:16,220
There he is. I see him!

1350
01:43:17,148 --> 01:43:18,357
Come on lets go.

1351
01:43:18,399 --> 01:43:19,136
Where is Sasha?

1352
01:43:19,160 --> 01:43:20,245
He said he's fine.

1353
01:43:20,443 --> 01:43:22,014
We should get out of here
before he touches down.

1354
01:43:22,038 --> 01:43:25,049
No, don't go! We should
wait for him No no no no.

1355
01:43:25,073 --> 01:43:26,751
Go Jackson, go.

1356
01:43:28,691 --> 01:43:29,691
It won't start.

1357
01:43:31,579 --> 01:43:33,748
Shut up everybody!

1358
01:43:35,468 --> 01:43:39,139
Engine start.

1359
01:43:42,256 --> 01:43:44,832
Voice control. Sold me on it.

1360
01:45:48,059 --> 01:45:50,572
Welcome, to the People's Republic of China.

1361
01:45:50,885 --> 01:45:52,981
Good to be here. Say hi, kids.

1362
01:45:54,712 --> 01:45:57,308
What color are your passes? What?

1363
01:45:57,694 --> 01:45:59,592
What color are your boarding passes?

1364
01:46:01,865 --> 01:46:03,304
I have green cards.

1365
01:46:04,409 --> 01:46:06,911
For my boys and me. What?

1366
01:46:11,114 --> 01:46:12,761
Yuri? Yuri!

1367
01:46:13,720 --> 01:46:16,379
Yuri. It's a mistake. A joke, eh?

1368
01:46:17,370 --> 01:46:22,886
What? You think I didn't
know about you and Sasha?

1369
01:46:23,981 --> 01:46:27,495
May God bless that poor bastard's soul.

1370
01:46:32,844 --> 01:46:35,805
I'm sorry guys. Good luck.

1371
01:46:37,202 --> 01:46:38,360
Come on, boys.

1372
01:46:40,508 --> 01:46:42,489
Maybe with money we
could bribe them. I do, I do.

1373
01:46:42,864 --> 01:46:44,313
You got a billion Euros?

1374
01:46:49,256 --> 01:46:50,256
Dr Wilson.

1375
01:46:51,018 --> 01:46:53,698
I'm captain Michaels,
skipper of the American ship.

1376
01:46:53,875 --> 01:46:56,114
Please accept my sincere
condolences for your father.

1377
01:46:56,138 --> 01:46:57,274
Thank you, captain.

1378
01:46:59,109 --> 01:47:02,060
Mr. Anheuser. Your
party is the last to arrive.

1379
01:47:06,492 --> 01:47:08,974
There's been reports of
severe damage, captain.

1380
01:47:09,099 --> 01:47:10,889
What's the status of ark number 3?

1381
01:47:10,913 --> 01:47:12,936
We haven't done a complete assessment yet.

1382
01:47:13,426 --> 01:47:15,032
Looks like we lost it.

1383
01:47:25,229 --> 01:47:27,471
No toothbrush. Only books.

1384
01:47:29,014 --> 01:47:31,705
When I was a kid my
Dad was on the road a lot.

1385
01:47:33,039 --> 01:47:34,934
He'd always leave me a box full of books.

1386
01:47:34,958 --> 01:47:36,584
Call me every night and cruise me.

1387
01:47:37,784 --> 01:47:40,390
I'd get an ice cream cone
for every book I read so.

1388
01:47:41,204 --> 01:47:42,403
I was a fat kid.

1389
01:47:43,936 --> 01:47:45,611
I find that very hard to believe.

1390
01:47:45,635 --> 01:47:47,783
No, its true, my high school career.

1391
01:47:47,898 --> 01:47:52,027
Was 2000 books zero girlfriends.

1392
01:47:53,873 --> 01:47:56,281
I didn't even kiss a boy
until I was in college.

1393
01:47:57,241 --> 01:47:59,107
They were all too scared of my dad.

1394
01:48:47,291 --> 01:48:48,719
Leave it to the Chinese.

1395
01:48:49,376 --> 01:48:50,700
I didn't think it was possible.

1396
01:48:51,076 --> 01:48:52,327
Not in the time we had.

1397
01:48:53,776 --> 01:48:55,226
That's ark number 3, sir.

1398
01:48:55,997 --> 01:48:59,157
The roof collapsed during
the shifting of the earth's crust.

1399
01:49:00,032 --> 01:49:01,513
Jesus Christ.

1400
01:49:02,869 --> 01:49:08,259
Boarding of arc 3 will be
delayed due to technical difficulties.

1401
01:49:11,419 --> 01:49:13,150
Hey, what's going on here?

1402
01:49:13,223 --> 01:49:15,806
I have a green card for my boys and me.

1403
01:49:15,830 --> 01:49:18,100
I want to speak to your supervisor.

1404
01:49:18,124 --> 01:49:19,559
I am the supervisor.

1405
01:49:19,583 --> 01:49:22,920
Get back with the other green
cards, or I'll have you detained.

1406
01:49:25,099 --> 01:49:26,976
What he said about
you and Sasha, is it true?

1407
01:49:27,477 --> 01:49:30,699
Sasha was worth a hundred
times a man like Yuri.

1408
01:49:31,543 --> 01:49:33,806
I should have listened
to you, Dr. Silberman.

1409
01:49:33,848 --> 01:49:36,444
I actually liked the way I looked before.

1410
01:49:36,475 --> 01:49:38,540
That monster talked me into it.

1411
01:49:39,103 --> 01:49:40,990
Did you know he asked me for a discount?

1412
01:49:41,418 --> 01:49:42,846
He payed in installments.

1413
01:49:43,253 --> 01:49:44,723
Cheap bastard.

1414
01:49:45,495 --> 01:49:46,495
You hear that?

1415
01:49:49,697 --> 01:49:50,719
Over there!

1416
01:49:54,597 --> 01:49:55,597
Stop!

1417
01:49:55,776 --> 01:49:56,776
Stop!

1418
01:50:00,895 --> 01:50:05,421
Hi! Hi! Stop! Stop the car.

1419
01:50:38,850 --> 01:50:40,529
How were all these people chosen?

1420
01:50:40,664 --> 01:50:41,819
Same way your arc was.

1421
01:50:41,843 --> 01:50:42,997
By experts from all over the world.

1422
01:50:43,021 --> 01:50:45,103
We had geneticists
determine the perfect gene pool.

1423
01:50:45,127 --> 01:50:46,104
We need to repopulate.

1424
01:50:46,128 --> 01:50:48,096
These people were chosen by geneticists?

1425
01:50:48,120 --> 01:50:52,267
All green card holders
please proceed to hangar D-4.

1426
01:50:52,291 --> 01:50:54,175
Looks to me like their check
books got them on board.

1427
01:50:54,199 --> 01:50:55,301
That's right, Dr. Wilson.

1428
01:50:55,325 --> 01:50:57,522
Without billions of dollars
from the private sector.

1429
01:50:57,546 --> 01:50:59,347
This entire operation
would've been impossible.

1430
01:50:59,371 --> 01:51:00,841
We sold tickets?

1431
01:51:01,592 --> 01:51:03,229
What about all these workers?

1432
01:51:03,844 --> 01:51:05,168
They all get passes?

1433
01:51:05,606 --> 01:51:08,234
What? Life isn't fair?

1434
01:51:08,557 --> 01:51:09,557
Is that it?

1435
01:51:09,756 --> 01:51:11,150
If you want to donate your passes,

1436
01:51:11,174 --> 01:51:12,683
To a couple of Chinese workers,

1437
01:51:12,707 --> 01:51:14,062
You be my guest.

1438
01:51:15,314 --> 01:51:16,836
Captain, I want a pre-launch briefing.

1439
01:51:16,878 --> 01:51:18,536
All international teams present.

1440
01:51:53,800 --> 01:51:55,187
What the hell?

1441
01:51:59,014 --> 01:52:01,860
What is this? They
could've fit 10 people in here.

1442
01:52:09,284 --> 01:52:10,525
Satnam, where are you?

1443
01:52:11,005 --> 01:52:13,737
On the Nampan Plateau. What?

1444
01:52:15,217 --> 01:52:17,247
There's a tidal wave coming from the east.

1445
01:52:17,271 --> 01:52:18,544
It's gigantic.

1446
01:52:18,981 --> 01:52:20,087
Satnam, what happened?

1447
01:52:20,754 --> 01:52:22,454
We never got picked up, Adrian.

1448
01:52:23,215 --> 01:52:24,518
The airlift never came.

1449
01:52:26,614 --> 01:52:27,813
Goodbye, my friend.

1450
01:52:29,273 --> 01:52:34,268
Satnam, Satnam.

1451
01:52:57,958 --> 01:53:00,502
Mary Where are we set up? Over there.

1452
01:53:05,434 --> 01:53:07,141
Give me the satellite
images from Nampan, India.

1453
01:53:07,165 --> 01:53:08,187
Ok, right away.

1454
01:53:08,635 --> 01:53:09,635
What's happening?

1455
01:53:10,533 --> 01:53:14,318
Satnam was talking about
another wave, coming from the east.

1456
01:53:18,291 --> 01:53:19,427
Holy mother of God.

1457
01:53:19,803 --> 01:53:22,427
So the flooding will hit earlier?

1458
01:53:22,451 --> 01:53:23,658
The second wave is closer?

1459
01:53:23,682 --> 01:53:24,818
Plug in the new data.

1460
01:53:26,914 --> 01:53:28,457
Satnam didn't get picked up.

1461
01:53:28,603 --> 01:53:29,354
What?

1462
01:53:29,531 --> 01:53:32,107
A lot of people didn't get
picked up in this chaos.

1463
01:53:32,555 --> 01:53:34,672
This is not a conspiracy, Helmsley.

1464
01:53:34,724 --> 01:53:38,519
Your predictions haven't exactly
panned out, have they, doctor?

1465
01:53:39,051 --> 01:53:40,051
It's ready.

1466
01:53:42,054 --> 01:53:43,785
Oh God, its 1500 meters high.

1467
01:53:45,380 --> 01:53:46,380
When will it get here?

1468
01:53:46,965 --> 01:53:48,474
Talk to me, Hemsley, when will it hit?

1469
01:53:48,498 --> 01:53:49,520
Adjust the countdown.

1470
01:54:06,506 --> 01:54:09,655
28 minutes, 10 seconds to impact.

1471
01:54:09,863 --> 01:54:10,863
My God.

1472
01:54:10,968 --> 01:54:11,968
Captain.

1473
01:54:12,678 --> 01:54:14,427
I need to speak to the other
heads of state immediately.

1474
01:54:14,451 --> 01:54:14,959
Right away.

1475
01:54:14,983 --> 01:54:17,117
Taylor? Aye, captain standing by.

1476
01:54:17,141 --> 01:54:19,807
Ark 6, stand by. Ark 7, stand by.

1477
01:54:19,831 --> 01:54:22,383
This is Carl Anheuser Acting CIC on 4,

1478
01:54:22,407 --> 01:54:23,019
Yes sir.

1479
01:54:23,043 --> 01:54:25,233
Requesting emergency conference T-99.

1480
01:54:46,337 --> 01:54:48,017
He thinks the world of you, you know that?

1481
01:54:50,862 --> 01:54:51,916
He's a great little man.

1482
01:54:53,490 --> 01:54:54,490
Yeah!

1483
01:55:02,958 --> 01:55:04,762
I always wanted to have a family of my own.

1484
01:55:09,141 --> 01:55:10,465
You're a lucky man, Jackson.

1485
01:55:12,040 --> 01:55:13,072
Don't ever forget it.

1486
01:55:29,641 --> 01:55:30,642
Who are they?

1487
01:55:31,403 --> 01:55:32,843
We found them alongside of the road.

1488
01:55:32,936 --> 01:55:34,875
Send them back!

1489
01:55:40,860 --> 01:55:45,188
I am a follower of our great lama Rinpoche.

1490
01:55:45,970 --> 01:55:47,398
You know I cannot do that.

1491
01:55:49,327 --> 01:55:50,554
You don't have to take all of us.

1492
01:55:50,578 --> 01:55:51,993
Please just take my children.

1493
01:55:52,017 --> 01:55:53,123
I'm begging you.

1494
01:55:53,540 --> 01:55:55,031
Why should I do that?

1495
01:55:55,521 --> 01:55:58,513
Same reason you sent for your family.

1496
01:55:58,785 --> 01:56:02,254
Please just the children,
you don't have to take us.

1497
01:56:02,278 --> 01:56:03,278
Please!

1498
01:56:06,501 --> 01:56:08,847
Please. Oh my God.

1499
01:56:12,361 --> 01:56:16,021
Please. I don't know if you
can understand what I'm saying.

1500
01:56:16,438 --> 01:56:18,489
As a mother, I'm begging you.

1501
01:56:18,513 --> 01:56:19,889
Please take them.

1502
01:56:21,380 --> 01:56:22,295
Please.

1503
01:56:22,319 --> 01:56:28,512
We are all children of the earth.

1504
01:56:29,305 --> 01:56:32,652
My plan will not work for so many, grandma.

1505
01:56:32,787 --> 01:56:35,644
We will take them all.

1506
01:56:52,223 --> 01:56:54,590
Attention. All construction workers.

1507
01:56:58,740 --> 01:57:00,628
They're opening the mountain.

1508
01:57:00,982 --> 01:57:03,526
They are leaving without us.

1509
01:57:05,038 --> 01:57:06,954
Get back. What did I tell you!

1510
01:57:06,978 --> 01:57:09,710
They are leaving you behind too.

1511
01:57:10,805 --> 01:57:12,191
Please be patient.

1512
01:57:19,970 --> 01:57:21,106
Follow me.

1513
01:57:24,464 --> 01:57:25,778
Follow me.

1514
01:57:33,223 --> 01:57:34,318
We have to hurry!

1515
01:57:34,818 --> 01:57:35,818
They are leaving!

1516
01:57:38,864 --> 01:57:40,824
Initiating security procedures.

1517
01:57:46,622 --> 01:57:49,131
Excuse me. Where can
I find Adrian Helmsley?

1518
01:57:49,155 --> 01:57:50,563
He's on the bridge. This way.

1519
01:57:54,911 --> 01:57:55,911
Tenzin wait!

1520
01:57:58,811 --> 01:57:59,600
Grandma, we're almost there.

1521
01:57:59,624 --> 01:58:01,720
Green lights on pressure, Mr. Anton?

1522
01:58:01,970 --> 01:58:03,530
Green lights across the board, captain.

1523
01:58:15,911 --> 01:58:17,194
Why do they have anchors?

1524
01:58:17,288 --> 01:58:20,103
Because they're not
space ships. They're arcs.

1525
01:58:20,875 --> 01:58:21,875
Let's go.

1526
01:58:34,628 --> 01:58:35,628
Mr president.

1527
01:58:36,682 --> 01:58:37,682
You've got to see this.

1528
01:59:08,798 --> 01:59:12,457
Stop.Stop.Stop.

1529
01:59:19,141 --> 01:59:20,935
Engage the support mechanisms.

1530
01:59:20,966 --> 01:59:23,090
Aye-aye, captain. Engaging supports.

1531
01:59:23,114 --> 01:59:26,082
Just exactly how long are these things
expected To hold us in place, Captain?

1532
01:59:26,106 --> 01:59:28,682
They're just meant to withstand
the first impact of the waves,

1533
01:59:28,724 --> 01:59:29,724
Mr Anheuser.

1534
01:59:47,253 --> 01:59:50,214
Down there Oleg, you go first.

1535
01:59:56,032 --> 01:59:57,032
Caesar!

1536
02:00:03,550 --> 02:00:04,550
Caesar!

1537
02:00:04,822 --> 02:00:06,094
Caesar!

1538
02:00:14,165 --> 02:00:16,699
Caesar! Caesar!

1539
02:00:17,835 --> 02:00:20,817
Good boy. Come to Mommy.

1540
02:00:21,391 --> 02:00:22,391
Caesar!

1541
02:00:23,268 --> 02:00:24,967
Mommy, where's Tamara?

1542
02:00:27,230 --> 02:00:28,534
Daddy look!

1543
02:00:32,235 --> 02:00:33,247
Tamara!

1544
02:01:10,325 --> 02:01:12,084
Oh my God, what's happening out there?

1545
02:01:12,108 --> 02:01:17,457
Anheuser convinced the
other Heads of state to launch.

1546
02:01:21,076 --> 02:01:22,129
Mr. Anheuser.

1547
02:01:24,454 --> 02:01:26,101
We have to stop this madness.

1548
02:01:27,405 --> 02:01:29,271
Make sure the other bridges can see me.

1549
02:01:30,116 --> 02:01:30,874
What do you think you're doing?

1550
02:01:30,898 --> 02:01:32,660
I know exactly what I'm doing. Turn it on.

1551
02:01:34,766 --> 02:01:35,399
Ladies and gentleman,

1552
02:01:35,423 --> 02:01:36,890
This is Dr. Adrian Helmsley.

1553
02:01:36,914 --> 02:01:39,813
Chief science adviser to
the late president Wilson.

1554
02:01:40,345 --> 02:01:42,357
Could you please turn up
the volume, Mr Hoffman.

1555
02:01:43,306 --> 02:01:44,408
I know we've all been forced to make.

1556
02:01:44,432 --> 02:01:47,195
Difficult decisions to
save our human civilization.

1557
02:01:47,592 --> 02:01:50,414
But to be human means
to care for each other and.

1558
02:01:50,438 --> 02:01:54,182
Civilization means to work
together to create a better life.

1559
02:01:54,703 --> 02:01:55,607
If that's true,

1560
02:01:55,631 --> 02:01:57,234
Then there's nothing human and.

1561
02:01:57,258 --> 02:01:59,966
Nothing civilized about
what we're doing here.

1562
02:01:59,990 --> 02:02:02,888
Dr. Helmsley's passion is admirable,

1563
02:02:03,076 --> 02:02:04,230
But I remind you that

1564
02:02:04,254 --> 02:02:07,306
we have very Limited resources
and extremely limited time.

1565
02:02:07,330 --> 02:02:07,984
Ask yourselves,

1566
02:02:08,008 --> 02:02:10,959
Can we really stand by
and watch these people die?

1567
02:02:12,815 --> 02:02:14,660
I read a quote two days ago.

1568
02:02:14,848 --> 02:02:16,711
The author is probably by now.

1569
02:02:16,735 --> 02:02:19,694
But he said that the moment
we stop fighting with each other.

1570
02:02:19,718 --> 02:02:23,023
"That's the moment that
we lose our humanity."

1571
02:02:23,211 --> 02:02:24,480
And in order to save the human race,

1572
02:02:24,504 --> 02:02:27,118
We have an obligation
to stick to this plan.

1573
02:02:27,142 --> 02:02:30,186
Which every nation on
this flotilla signed up for.

1574
02:02:30,405 --> 02:02:32,105
They're in God's hands now.

1575
02:02:34,712 --> 02:02:36,547
Officer, you turn that off.

1576
02:02:38,184 --> 02:02:39,536
That is an order, sailor. Turn it off!

1577
02:02:39,560 --> 02:02:41,406
Don't you dare touch
that button, young man!

1578
02:02:41,469 --> 02:02:43,929
Have you completely lost your mind?

1579
02:02:44,524 --> 02:02:45,691
Look at the clock!

1580
02:02:45,837 --> 02:02:47,902
We have barely 15 minutes left!

1581
02:02:48,361 --> 02:02:50,808
Do you want to be responsible for
the extinction of the human race?

1582
02:02:50,832 --> 02:02:52,167
Can you handle that, Adrian?

1583
02:02:53,022 --> 02:02:55,104
There's a young astrophysicist from India

1584
02:02:55,128 --> 02:02:56,637
who's the reason we are all here.

1585
02:02:56,661 --> 02:02:57,881
Oh, for God's sake.

1586
02:02:58,433 --> 02:03:00,787
He's the one who discovered it all.

1587
02:03:00,811 --> 02:03:01,965
He connected all the dots,

1588
02:03:01,989 --> 02:03:03,991
We all owe him our lives.

1589
02:03:04,721 --> 02:03:06,970
I just learned that he
was killed with His family

1590
02:03:06,994 --> 02:03:09,517
in a tsunami in eastern India.

1591
02:03:12,051 --> 02:03:13,375
He was my friend.

1592
02:03:14,637 --> 02:03:16,003
And he died in vain.

1593
02:03:17,327 --> 02:03:20,640
Everybody out there has died in vain.

1594
02:03:20,664 --> 02:03:23,917
If we start our future
with an act of cruelty,

1595
02:03:25,940 --> 02:03:27,525
What will you tell your children?

1596
02:03:34,042 --> 02:03:35,533
If my father were here,

1597
02:03:36,086 --> 02:03:37,545
He would open the gates.

1598
02:03:44,928 --> 02:03:52,928
The people of Russia along withChina
and Japan agree to open the gates!

1599
02:03:59,839 --> 02:04:02,351
The United Kingdom, Spain, France

1600
02:04:02,602 --> 02:04:04,246
Canada and Germany,

1601
02:04:04,270 --> 02:04:08,357
And I believe I may also
speak for the Italy president.

1602
02:04:08,764 --> 02:04:11,110
The we vote to let these people come in.

1603
02:04:17,690 --> 02:04:21,548
Captain Michaels. Please.

1604
02:04:26,136 --> 02:04:27,147
This is your captain.

1605
02:04:27,773 --> 02:04:30,223
In a few moments, we will open the gates.

1606
02:04:38,502 --> 02:04:40,473
Phew, it stinks.

1607
02:04:59,763 --> 02:05:01,136
They are opening the gate.

1608
02:05:01,160 --> 02:05:03,402
Come down! Noah. Move it!

1609
02:05:04,320 --> 02:05:06,332
Noah! Noah! Noah!

1610
02:05:17,635 --> 02:05:19,230
Mom, something happened.

1611
02:05:19,814 --> 02:05:21,410
Hold on, hold on.

1612
02:05:24,277 --> 02:05:29,634
Hold on, god damn it! Give me your hand!

1613
02:05:29,658 --> 02:05:30,801
Give me your hand! Give me your hand!

1614
02:05:30,825 --> 02:05:33,881
Reach for it! Help me!

1615
02:05:36,936 --> 02:05:37,937
Gordon!

1616
02:05:40,971 --> 02:05:41,971
Stop!

1617
02:05:47,540 --> 02:05:48,540
Climb!

1618
02:06:22,825 --> 02:06:23,905
What's wrong with the gate?

1619
02:06:24,202 --> 02:06:25,481
Looks like it didn't run the full cycle.

1620
02:06:25,505 --> 02:06:26,569
We're checking it out.

1621
02:06:28,164 --> 02:06:29,238
Order, please!

1622
02:06:36,255 --> 02:06:37,726
4 minutes to impact.

1623
02:07:24,178 --> 02:07:26,723
We're all loaded, captain.
Then let's lock it up. Now!

1624
02:07:37,306 --> 02:07:39,756
Oleg! Grab my hand!

1625
02:07:40,445 --> 02:07:41,831
Oleg!

1626
02:07:41,863 --> 02:07:43,865
No, no, no.

1627
02:07:46,325 --> 02:07:48,192
No!

1628
02:08:12,560 --> 02:08:14,100
Something's jamming
the hydraulics, Captain.

1629
02:08:14,124 --> 02:08:15,591
Well then get it out for Christ sake.

1630
02:08:15,615 --> 02:08:18,576
I can't fire up the engines until
we get a good seal on that gate.

1631
02:08:19,067 --> 02:08:21,360
Captain, we have a
breach in the zoological bay.

1632
02:08:21,465 --> 02:08:22,465
Can you zoom in?

1633
02:08:22,507 --> 02:08:23,507
Yeah!

1634
02:08:27,773 --> 02:08:28,688
I know those kids.

1635
02:08:28,712 --> 02:08:31,235
What is happening? What's going on?

1636
02:08:31,548 --> 02:08:32,684
Where did they come from?

1637
02:08:35,416 --> 02:08:37,259
There. Through the hydraulic chamber.

1638
02:08:37,283 --> 02:08:38,833
Captain, I think we found the problem!

1639
02:08:38,857 --> 02:08:40,692
Who are these people? No, wait!

1640
02:08:41,714 --> 02:08:42,715
He's injured.

1641
02:08:42,892 --> 02:08:44,109
Something must've gone wrong.

1642
02:08:44,133 --> 02:08:45,624
Something must've gone wrong?

1643
02:08:46,135 --> 02:08:49,326
Are you kidding me? Of
course something went wrong!

1644
02:08:49,701 --> 02:08:51,370
Congratulations to the both of you.

1645
02:08:51,630 --> 02:08:52,753
Might have gotten us all killed,

1646
02:08:52,777 --> 02:08:55,217
But as long as your conscience
is clean, right Helmsley?

1647
02:08:55,280 --> 02:08:56,872
Captain, get an emergency team down there

1648
02:08:56,896 --> 02:08:58,616
I'll meet them at the hydraulics chamber.

1649
02:08:58,762 --> 02:09:00,907
You know your way
around here? Yeah. Let's go!

1650
02:09:00,931 --> 02:09:03,006
1 minute to impact.

1651
02:09:16,968 --> 02:09:17,968
Captain?

1652
02:09:18,219 --> 02:09:19,721
Cho Ming airfield has been hit.

1653
02:09:20,482 --> 02:09:22,536
Put me on emergency comm, Mr.Taylor.

1654
02:09:25,216 --> 02:09:30,158
This is the captain speaking we
expect to be impacted by water shortly.

1655
02:09:30,430 --> 02:09:31,430
We need to go this way.

1656
02:09:53,150 --> 02:09:55,517
All stations prepare for impact.

1657
02:10:42,053 --> 02:10:44,326
Pressure just climbed 80 Pascal.

1658
02:10:44,420 --> 02:10:47,128
Surface compression of
valve sensors, Captain.

1659
02:10:47,152 --> 02:10:48,466
Track Dr Helmsley.

1660
02:10:48,966 --> 02:10:49,966
There.

1661
02:10:54,628 --> 02:10:56,609
Out of the way! Excuse me.

1662
02:10:58,069 --> 02:11:00,332
Tenzin. Almost there.

1663
02:11:01,208 --> 02:11:02,615
Nima. What happened?

1664
02:11:05,181 --> 02:11:05,921
Tamara!

1665
02:11:06,192 --> 02:11:08,361
Will you take the kids please?

1666
02:11:08,747 --> 02:11:09,747
Which way?

1667
02:11:10,196 --> 02:11:13,845
We can't get there!
Water is entering the stern.

1668
02:11:14,461 --> 02:11:18,141
The rear of this ship is flooded and
Will seal up one compartment at a time.

1669
02:11:18,850 --> 02:11:19,850
Where's Gordon?

1670
02:11:21,353 --> 02:11:22,353
No?

1671
02:11:24,377 --> 02:11:25,377
We gotta go back!

1672
02:11:26,056 --> 02:11:28,068
We have to go back!

1673
02:11:31,728 --> 02:11:33,115
Mommy!

1674
02:11:33,448 --> 02:11:35,753
Help! Mommy!

1675
02:11:37,557 --> 02:11:39,308
Run!

1676
02:11:40,695 --> 02:11:41,717
Lilly run!

1677
02:11:44,866 --> 02:11:46,138
Go over, Lilly!

1678
02:11:49,152 --> 02:11:51,185
Caesar! Lilly, take him!

1679
02:11:53,886 --> 02:11:55,439
Mommy!

1680
02:12:02,540 --> 02:12:05,248
Is there another way to
the hydraulics chamber?

1681
02:12:05,272 --> 02:12:06,207
Where does this ladder go?

1682
02:12:06,231 --> 02:12:09,286
To the zoological pens Okay, let's go!

1683
02:12:15,543 --> 02:12:18,274
Professor? It's Air Force One.

1684
02:12:36,407 --> 02:12:37,718
The mid-ship anchor support is hit.

1685
02:12:37,742 --> 02:12:39,084
Can you stabilize it?

1686
02:12:39,108 --> 02:12:40,714
The bow anchor is giving in.

1687
02:13:00,546 --> 02:13:02,357
Captain, the turbines aren't responding.

1688
02:13:02,381 --> 02:13:05,225
So override it. Hit the
override. Start the engine.

1689
02:13:05,249 --> 02:13:07,543
We can't start the engine
until we close that gate.

1690
02:13:26,092 --> 02:13:28,105
Help me! Help!

1691
02:13:33,266 --> 02:13:34,611
Momma!

1692
02:13:35,060 --> 02:13:37,166
Momma!

1693
02:13:37,823 --> 02:13:40,499
Are you ok? My Mommy
is in there. Please help her!

1694
02:13:40,523 --> 02:13:41,553
We'll get to your Mommy, sweetheart.

1695
02:13:41,577 --> 02:13:42,929
They're doing everything they can, okay?

1696
02:13:42,953 --> 02:13:44,121
Can we talk to her?

1697
02:13:44,256 --> 02:13:45,664
I'm gonna try to connect us.

1698
02:13:46,456 --> 02:13:47,892
We have to stop the bleeding!

1699
02:13:47,916 --> 02:13:49,188
How about my belt?

1700
02:13:49,459 --> 02:13:52,056
Here Mom! Mr. Curtis? Jackson?

1701
02:13:52,598 --> 02:13:55,465
Help!

1702
02:13:55,757 --> 02:13:57,926
It's Adrian Helmsley,
we met at Yellowstone.

1703
02:13:58,020 --> 02:14:00,543
That's great. Open the god damn door!

1704
02:14:00,867 --> 02:14:02,024
Your daughter is with me!

1705
02:14:02,149 --> 02:14:05,663
Lilly? Where's Noah?

1706
02:14:05,851 --> 02:14:07,071
I'm right here, Lil!

1707
02:14:07,769 --> 02:14:13,272
Impact warning 30 west. 45 east.

1708
02:14:13,296 --> 02:14:17,036
Target elevation 29035 feet.

1709
02:14:17,060 --> 02:14:20,198
29000 feet? What the hell is at 29000 feet?

1710
02:14:20,501 --> 02:14:23,136
We're headed straight for
the north face of Mount Everest

1711
02:14:23,160 --> 02:14:24,536
Mr. Anheuser.

1712
02:14:24,943 --> 02:14:28,895
And if we can't start our engines,
we will not survive the impact.

1713
02:14:39,374 --> 02:14:42,408
Jackson, you're sealed
off! We can't get to you!

1714
02:14:42,523 --> 02:14:44,345
There's something blocking the hydraulics.

1715
02:14:44,369 --> 02:14:46,746
If you can't get it out, none
of us are gonna make it.

1716
02:14:48,341 --> 02:14:50,562
Dr. Helmsley, look at this.

1717
02:14:51,313 --> 02:14:52,895
It's completely submerged down there.

1718
02:14:52,919 --> 02:14:55,213
And there's no way for them to get any air.

1719
02:14:55,338 --> 02:14:56,338
Theres no other way!

1720
02:14:56,474 --> 02:14:58,320
But it's a suicide mission, Sir!

1721
02:15:06,026 --> 02:15:07,923
I know where it is, I'll give it a try.

1722
02:15:15,097 --> 02:15:17,360
Dad, wait, I wanna go with you!

1723
02:15:17,495 --> 02:15:19,925
Dad, I wanna help you! No, no, no.

1724
02:15:20,425 --> 02:15:22,344
You are helping me. Dad, please!

1725
02:15:22,407 --> 02:15:24,711
Remember when Lilly was born.

1726
02:15:24,899 --> 02:15:26,939
And you wanted to be
introduced as her big brother?

1727
02:15:27,276 --> 02:15:28,444
Well, she's scared now.

1728
02:15:28,600 --> 02:15:30,070
She needs you more than ever.

1729
02:15:30,540 --> 02:15:33,584
If you're safe, I know that
she's safe. Do you understand?

1730
02:15:40,550 --> 02:15:42,155
You can help me out the next time.

1731
02:15:45,982 --> 02:15:47,484
We caused this thing, it was us.

1732
02:15:47,797 --> 02:15:48,954
I gotta go check it out.

1733
02:16:19,547 --> 02:16:21,122
Can you hear me?

1734
02:16:27,930 --> 02:16:30,256
Who can help me! Help!

1735
02:16:32,873 --> 02:16:34,353
Who can help me!

1736
02:16:53,289 --> 02:16:54,321
Press down!

1737
02:16:54,478 --> 02:16:56,115
Press down with your hand!

1738
02:17:04,415 --> 02:17:06,229
Don't stop. Keep pressing!

1739
02:17:23,788 --> 02:17:25,175
No!

1740
02:17:29,106 --> 02:17:33,496
Distance to impact 1850 meters.

1741
02:17:36,290 --> 02:17:37,302
There he is!

1742
02:17:38,855 --> 02:17:40,948
Captain! We have a visual!

1743
02:17:40,972 --> 02:17:42,463
I think we found the problem.

1744
02:17:42,578 --> 02:17:43,986
Show us the hydraulics chamber.

1745
02:18:01,649 --> 02:18:03,794
I told you to stay up there with your Mom!

1746
02:18:03,818 --> 02:18:05,205
I just wanted to help.

1747
02:18:07,280 --> 02:18:08,872
Alright. Hold the light.

1748
02:18:08,896 --> 02:18:10,523
We're right under the air pocket, okay?

1749
02:18:11,576 --> 02:18:12,816
How did you know I needed help?

1750
02:18:17,592 --> 02:18:20,720
Grandpa, grandmal'm sorry.

1751
02:18:21,930 --> 02:18:22,930
I could not save us.

1752
02:18:23,536 --> 02:18:26,445
He has gone back in. He will fix it.

1753
02:18:27,373 --> 02:18:29,448
There's no way.

1754
02:18:30,563 --> 02:18:32,492
Don't lose faith, brother.

1755
02:19:08,007 --> 02:19:09,007
Malfunction.

1756
02:19:10,166 --> 02:19:12,282
We're gonna die! We're gonna die!

1757
02:19:33,668 --> 02:19:36,536
Great job! You light the
way and I'll go for the cable.

1758
02:19:37,808 --> 02:19:40,286
Distance to impact 400 meters.

1759
02:19:40,310 --> 02:19:41,895
Underwater ridge ahead!

1760
02:19:41,947 --> 02:19:43,428
We're going to run aground, captain!

1761
02:20:13,844 --> 02:20:15,429
Sir, the gate is sealed!

1762
02:20:15,554 --> 02:20:16,719
That's affirmative, captain!

1763
02:20:16,743 --> 02:20:18,356
Anton, start the engines.

1764
02:20:18,380 --> 02:20:20,267
Aye-aye captain. Full reverse.

1765
02:20:29,078 --> 02:20:30,733
Captain! We're not gonna make it!

1766
02:20:30,757 --> 02:20:33,415
Distance to impact 50 meters.

1767
02:20:34,281 --> 02:20:35,605
40 meters.

1768
02:20:59,129 --> 02:21:01,162
Reverse motion activated.

1769
02:21:01,485 --> 02:21:07,001
10 meters. 20 meters.

1770
02:21:21,505 --> 02:21:22,326
Hard to port!

1771
02:21:22,350 --> 02:21:23,872
Okay, hard to port!

1772
02:21:35,029 --> 02:21:37,553
We did it! We did it!

1773
02:21:38,272 --> 02:21:40,222
Where's Dad? He was right behind me, Mommy.

1774
02:21:42,015 --> 02:21:44,069
Any word from the hydraulic chamber?

1775
02:21:44,226 --> 02:21:45,039
Where is he?

1776
02:21:45,216 --> 02:21:46,923
I thought you said he was right behind you.

1777
02:21:46,947 --> 02:21:47,719
He was!

1778
02:21:47,813 --> 02:21:49,241
Are you sure? Yes.

1779
02:21:49,533 --> 02:21:50,993
He was right there!

1780
02:21:59,543 --> 02:22:02,880
Dad. Dad!

1781
02:22:03,360 --> 02:22:04,924
Come on, Jackson. Come on.

1782
02:22:09,397 --> 02:22:11,733
Please, please.

1783
02:22:14,047 --> 02:22:16,706
Please, please.

1784
02:22:34,265 --> 02:22:35,265
He did it!

1785
02:22:36,038 --> 02:22:37,038
He did it!

1786
02:23:35,837 --> 02:23:38,163
Shuttle Atlantis. Our last day.

1787
02:23:39,049 --> 02:23:41,896
All we can hear is the
sound of our own breathing.

1788
02:23:42,073 --> 02:23:45,532
That reminds us we are
still sharing our memories.

1789
02:23:45,556 --> 02:23:47,234
Hopes and ideas.

1790
02:23:48,048 --> 02:23:51,019
And isn't it funny? Just
this morning, we walked out.

1791
02:23:51,708 --> 02:23:55,899
Somehow we all have relatives in Wisconsin.

1792
02:23:58,944 --> 02:23:59,944
The end.

1793
02:24:10,341 --> 02:24:11,341
It's good.

1794
02:24:12,603 --> 02:24:13,803
I thought you would like it.

1795
02:24:15,898 --> 02:24:20,007
Tell meApart from books and art.

1796
02:24:21,873 --> 02:24:24,928
Do you think there's anything
else we might possibly share?

1797
02:24:25,804 --> 02:24:26,889
In the future?

1798
02:24:28,557 --> 02:24:31,675
Are you asking me out
on a date, Dr. Helmsley?

1799
02:24:33,072 --> 02:24:35,230
You know my diary is pretty full.

1800
02:24:37,118 --> 02:24:38,118
Actually.

1801
02:24:41,518 --> 02:24:42,571
Yes, I was.

1802
02:24:47,586 --> 02:24:49,474
Dr. Helmsley to the bridge, please.

1803
02:24:50,537 --> 02:24:51,997
Dr. Helmsley to the bridge.

1804
02:24:54,812 --> 02:24:55,812
Come here.

1805
02:25:02,445 --> 02:25:04,801
Ladies and gentleman, this
is captain Michaels speaking.

1806
02:25:05,802 --> 02:25:09,087
In a few minutes I will give
orders to unseal the decks.

1807
02:25:10,338 --> 02:25:12,295
At 23:45 last night.

1808
02:25:12,319 --> 02:25:16,636
Our sister arks number 6
and 7 have joined our course.

1809
02:25:18,075 --> 02:25:22,569
For the first time on our
journey, we will have clear skies.

1810
02:25:23,278 --> 02:25:26,469
As you know our passenger
count is way over capacity.

1811
02:25:26,615 --> 02:25:30,306
So please, be careful when
you step out and of course.

1812
02:25:30,754 --> 02:25:32,381
Enjoy the fresh air.

1813
02:25:35,426 --> 02:25:36,426
Can I hold him?

1814
02:25:36,896 --> 02:25:39,576
Sure, he can be your dog too if you like.

1815
02:25:39,670 --> 02:25:40,670
Thanks.

1816
02:25:45,019 --> 02:25:46,299
Where have you been all my life?

1817
02:25:46,625 --> 02:25:47,625
Gift shop.

1818
02:26:45,319 --> 02:26:47,884
Oh, Adrian. Excellent.

1819
02:26:48,040 --> 02:26:50,279
I called because we just
got our first satellite feet.

1820
02:26:50,303 --> 02:26:52,221
The equalization of the oceanic.

1821
02:26:52,419 --> 02:26:56,191
Seabeds has not turned out to
be as extreme as we expected.

1822
02:26:56,215 --> 02:26:57,623
The waters are receding.

1823
02:26:57,654 --> 02:26:59,082
Much faster than we thought.

1824
02:26:59,124 --> 02:27:00,605
Thank God. And.

1825
02:27:01,241 --> 02:27:02,103
This is hard to believe,

1826
02:27:02,127 --> 02:27:04,995
But the Himalayas are no
longer the roof of the world.

1827
02:27:05,234 --> 02:27:08,703
It's now the Drakensberg
Mountains of Kwazulu, Nepal.

1828
02:27:08,727 --> 02:27:10,851
The entire African
continent has just risen.

1829
02:27:10,875 --> 02:27:14,014
7000 feet, and unlikely
they are even flooded.

1830
02:27:14,066 --> 02:27:16,086
That's why they call it
the Cape of Good Hope.

1831
02:27:16,110 --> 02:27:17,809
We've already set course for it.

1832
02:27:25,703 --> 02:27:27,736
Daddy, when will we go back home?

1833
02:27:28,518 --> 02:27:29,808
Well, we talked about that.

1834
02:27:29,832 --> 02:27:31,980
We're gonna find a new
home out here somewhere.

1835
02:27:33,096 --> 02:27:35,671
Right? Wherever we're
all together. That's home.

1836
02:27:36,714 --> 02:27:37,714
Right?

1837
02:27:38,299 --> 02:27:39,299
You are scared?

1838
02:27:39,341 --> 02:27:40,341
I am not.

1839
02:27:42,553 --> 02:27:44,013
No more pull-ups.

1840
02:27:47,381 --> 02:27:48,381
Nice.

